IoT project he worked on,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.810
which was in conjunction
with Firebase.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.460
And so he wanted to--

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.240
he's a musician on the side.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.684
And there's a sound room that
he wanted to be able to have

00:02:55.684 --> 00:02:58.100
an understanding of when it's
available and when it isn't.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.570
So he built out an IoT
device using a Raspberry Pi

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:06.370
and Passive Infrared sensor
to detect motion and determine

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.260
when the room is in use.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.360
And he was doing this
with a motion sensor

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.840
to avoid capturing sound or
capturing video in that room,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.090
but to definitely
detect, is it in use

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.830
and how often is it in use?

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.262
And he shows how to build that
out with the actual IoT device,

00:03:21.262 --> 00:03:23.470
as well as combine it with
Firebase to track the data

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:23.970
itself.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.752
So you should check
out the blog posts

00:03:25.752 --> 00:03:28.210
